{"name":"Iced Slate","hex":"#d6dcd7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"iced","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["With ice added.","Very cold, but not necessarily containing ice."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of ice"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/iced"},{"term":"slate","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flake or piece of certain types of stone that tend to cleave into thin layers.\n A piece of such stone, usually cut into a rectangular shape, used as a tile for flooring, roofing, etc.;  such tiles collectively, or the material from which they are made.\n\nA piece of other material used as a roofing tile.","A piece of such stone, usually cut into a rectangular shape, used as a tile for flooring, roofing, etc.;  such tiles collectively, or the material from which they are made."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the bluish-grey colour of slate (noun etymology 1, noun sense 4)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slate"}],"entries":[{"title":"Slate","blocks":[{"text":"Slate is a fine-grained, foliated, homogeneous, metamorphic rock derived from an original shale-type sedimentary rock composed of clay or volcanic ash through low-grade, regional metamorphism. It is the finest-grained foliated metamorphic rock. Foliation may not correspond to the original sedimentary layering, but instead is in planes perpendicular to the direction of metamorphic compression."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Slate_%28Knife_Lake_Formation%2C_metamorphism_at_2.7_Ga%2C_Neoarchean%3B_Rt._135_roadcut%2C_Gilbert%2C_Minnesota%2C_USA%29_3_%2823140002749%29.jpg/330px-Slate_%28Knife_Lake_Formation%2C_metamorphism_at_2.7_Ga%2C_Neoarchean%3B_Rt._135_roadcut%2C_Gilbert%2C_Minnesota%2C_USA%29_3_%2823140002749%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slate","wikidata":"Q207079"},{"title":"Slate gray","blocks":[{"text":"Slate gray is a moderate shade of gray with a slight azure tinge, which represents the average color of slate, a metamorphic rock often used in stonemasonry. As a tertiary color, slate is an equal mix of purple and green pigments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/St_Fagans_Tannery_7.jpg/330px-St_Fagans_Tannery_7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slate_gray","wikidata":"Q1411452"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Slate_with_pyrite.JPG/500px-Slate_with_pyrite.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Slate_with_pyrite.JPG/1280px-Slate_with_pyrite.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Slate_with_pyrite.JPG/500px-Slate_with_pyrite.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Slate with pyrite","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASlate_with_pyrite.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Slate_outcrop_Porto_Covo_August_2026-7.jpg/500px-Slate_outcrop_Porto_Covo_August_2026-7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Slate_outcrop_Porto_Covo_August_2026-7.jpg/1280px-Slate_outcrop_Porto_Covo_August_2026-7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Slate_outcrop_Porto_Covo_August_2026-7.jpg/500px-Slate_outcrop_Porto_Covo_August_2026-7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Detail of a slate outcrop at the beach of Porto Covo, Portugal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.or